WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.235
-My first guest tonight is
an Emmy-winning comedian

00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:05.437
who you know
from "Saturday Night Live,"

00:00:05.437 --> 00:00:08.408
which is all new this week
with host Dave Chappelle

00:00:08.408 --> 00:00:10.443
and musical guest --
[ Cheering ]

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:12.345
musical guest Foo Fighters.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:14.313
[ Cheers and applause ]
Come on!

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:16.750
You can also see him
in the movie "Hubie Halloween,"

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:18.851
which is so funny, man.
He's great.

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:20.520
It's available now on Netflix.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.089
Everyone, please welcome
Kenan Thompson.

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.557
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:26.993
-♪ We love Kenan Thompson ♪

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.194
♪♪

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.396
♪ Saturday Night, SNL ♪

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:32.131
♪♪

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:35.601
♪ We love Kenan Thompson ♪

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:37.904
♪ He got soul
hear to tell ♪

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:43.176
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:43.176 --> 00:00:44.711
-We don't play
entrance music anymore.

00:00:44.711 --> 00:00:46.112
That is all new.
What was that?

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:47.313
♪ Kenan Thompson ♪

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:48.814
-Made it up.
-Just made up the song.

00:00:48.814 --> 00:00:51.684
-[ Vocalizing ]

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.252
-♪ Kenan Thompson ♪

00:00:53.252 --> 00:00:55.254
-[ Both vocalizing ]

00:00:55.254 --> 00:00:56.956
-♪ Kenan Thompson ♪

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.458
-Musicians, man.
-I know.

00:00:58.458 --> 00:00:59.559
-You guys are the best, man.

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:00.926
Shout out to Philly,
by the way.

00:01:00.926 --> 00:01:02.795
You know what I'm talking about?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:07.333
-You know, Kenan does the
warm-up before the audience --

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.235
before the show starts on
"Saturday Night Live."

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.537
And it's right up to
the last second.

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:13.906
Usually do standup or you
do a song with the band.

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:16.242
Or I did -- I used to do
Rolling Stones

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:18.244
when I was on the show.
-Which song?

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:20.746
-I did "Midnight Rambler."
-Which goes?

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:24.450
-No, no, no, no, I can't.
That's too much money.

00:01:24.450 --> 00:01:26.585
-Is that really?
-We can't afford Rolling Stones.

00:01:26.585 --> 00:01:27.987
-Can't even just replay the --
-No.

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.855
We can do like a different
version of the song.

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:31.824
-That's amazing.
But, yeah, no, we warm up

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.460
the crowd before the show.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:36.629
And Michael Che does some
good stand-up

00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:39.832
and he introduces me
and I force karaoke upon --

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:41.934
upon the crowd.

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.302
But it's a good time.

00:01:43.302 --> 00:01:45.238
You know, it's good to
get the energy up.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:48.641
And I get my little jitters out
from seeing people staring at me

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.243
and stuff like that.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.111
-Get your nerves out.
I remember I did --

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:54.213
I worked -- I did such --

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:56.982
I really went for
this song so hard.

00:01:56.982 --> 00:01:58.518
And I was pretending I was
Mick Jagger --

00:01:58.518 --> 00:01:59.919
-You were playing.
-And Keith Richards.

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:01.454
I was playing the guitar
and singing,

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:02.921
then I laid on the ground.
I flipped --

00:02:02.921 --> 00:02:05.558
You know, this is pro-COVID.
I was laying on people.

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:07.160
-This is before the show
even starts?

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.495
-Before the show even started.
And then I was in a sketch,

00:02:09.495 --> 00:02:10.997
the cold open sketch.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:02:10.997 --> 00:02:12.665
-And so they go,
"We're starting in, you know,

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.601
five seconds."
You know? And you go --

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:16.035
-Voice blown.
-Yup.

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.436
-My voice is blown every week.
-Sweaty.

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:18.671
-Yeah.
-Dude, I was in --

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:20.573
Tina was like,
"What is wrong with you?"

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:22.541
I go --
[ Panting ]

00:02:22.541 --> 00:02:24.843
-"And live from New York --"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.843 --> 00:02:26.645
-"Hold on a second.
Rachel, you say it.

00:02:26.645 --> 00:02:28.114
You say it. I can't talk."
-It's intense.

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:31.117
But, I mean -- but, you know,
it's a specific kind of love

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:33.352
you have for entertaining,
I think, you know?

00:02:33.352 --> 00:02:34.920
-Yeah.
-And that comes through

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.523
when you're, I guess,
chosen to be in that role

00:02:37.523 --> 00:02:40.659
of even warming up the audience
before we do an awesome show.

00:02:40.659 --> 00:02:42.562
-Yeah. 'Cause it's like --
"Yeah, we want this show

00:02:42.562 --> 00:02:44.230
to be -- we're a team."
-Yeah, man.

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.165
-We want everyone to score.
-I want everybody to experience

00:02:46.165 --> 00:02:47.566
a good time, you know?
-Yeah.

00:02:47.566 --> 00:02:49.469
-I wish it could be always --
-And this week --

00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:51.704
-Shout out to those talented
people that we just saw.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:52.939
That was -- that was incredible.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.273
-Yeah.
That was amazing, right?

00:02:54.273 --> 00:02:55.675
[ Applause ]
-Incredible.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:57.376
-Isn't that cool?
-All three of them

00:02:57.376 --> 00:03:00.346
were very -- I thought it was
funny how she stubbed her toe

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.081
a little less
after that first one.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.749
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.749 --> 00:03:06.085
-She got a little bit too real.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:06.085 --> 00:03:07.553
It's like, "Ooh,
that was a really --"

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:08.988
Yeah, method actor.
-Yeah. That was incredible.

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:11.590
And all the way from Italy.
Come on.

00:03:11.590 --> 00:03:14.494
The global unite.

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:16.829
-You have Dave Chappelle
hosting this Saturday.

00:03:16.829 --> 00:03:18.998
-Whew!
-First of all, it's the sixth--

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:21.134
Yeah, I mean, come on.
[ Applause ]

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:24.737
But a six-show run
is pretty amazing,

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.206
and to end it with
Dave Chappelle who's just,

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:29.575
I mean, brilliant.
-Come on. I mean, who better?

00:03:29.575 --> 00:03:30.743
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:33.112
Especially since
it's a resurgence

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:35.181
of the last four year
when he made his appearance.

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:36.916
You know what I mean?
-Was that four years?

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:38.350
-Yeah.
-Geez.

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:40.420
-And it was, you know,
just an electric week then.

00:03:40.420 --> 00:03:43.189
So I know the show Saturday
is going to be powerful.

00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:44.857
It's going to be very,
very powerful.

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:47.727
So -- I'm going to be honest.
He complimented us yesterday.

00:03:47.727 --> 00:03:50.296
He made an insane speech, you
know, before the table read.

00:03:50.296 --> 00:03:52.999
Did the same thing years ago.

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:55.868
But I mean, the guy is just such
a prolific speaker.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.202
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:57.202 --> 00:03:59.538
And he speaks from the heart,
and a brilliant mind.

00:03:59.538 --> 00:04:01.707
And it's such a pleasure
to be around.

00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:03.776
I mean, y'all know.
-Yeah.

00:04:03.776 --> 00:04:05.911
Yeah, you went to his thing
in -- in Ohio, right?

00:04:05.911 --> 00:04:07.180
-That's right.

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.615
-That's -- he's just -- I --
he's like a -- beyond --

00:04:09.615 --> 00:04:11.184
I don't want to say wordsmith,
it's beyond that.

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:13.185
He's a poet. He's like --
it's so many things.

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:14.654
But funny.

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:17.823
Dude, I remember back in the day
when we --

00:04:17.823 --> 00:04:19.625
I used to do stand-up
and see him.

00:04:19.625 --> 00:04:22.061
This is when -- does he still
smoke on stage?

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.830
-Constantly.
-Yeah.

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:25.698
-He smoked more than
I've ever seen,

00:04:25.698 --> 00:04:28.334
and he was like -- and just
lighting up the whole thing.

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:30.169
And this was like --
I don't know what --

00:04:30.169 --> 00:04:31.571
I guess if they banned
cigarettes,

00:04:31.571 --> 00:04:33.306
that have a weird scene.
-Yeah.

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.174
He almost does it on purpose,
I feel like now.

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.743
-Exactly, yeah.

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:39.178
Keith Richards was here, and he
smoked and the alarms went off.

00:04:39.178 --> 00:04:40.412
-Yeah.

00:04:40.412 --> 00:04:41.647
-And I went into
his dressing room.

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:43.349
-"Isn't this this cool?"
-Yeah. No, I said to him,

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:44.817
I go, "Keith, you know
you can't smoke."

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.285
He goes, "I know, it's bad
for your health, right?"

00:04:46.285 --> 00:04:47.587
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.587 --> 00:04:49.422
He knows what's up.
It's Keith Richards, man.

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:51.891
-He's fine. He'll be fine.
-Can you -- look at this.

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:53.459
That's you --
-Look at that.

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:58.765
-Tracy Morgan, Eddie Murphy,
Chris rock, Dave Chappelle.

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:00.767
What was this feeling like?

00:05:00.767 --> 00:05:02.968
-First of all, it was
the Christmas show,

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:04.637
so Merry Christmas to me.

00:05:04.637 --> 00:05:07.140
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.574
-Yeah.
-Those guys --

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:10.542
those are four legends
I'm standing next to.

00:05:10.542 --> 00:05:12.711
You know what I'm saying?
You know, going down the line,

00:05:12.711 --> 00:05:14.680
Tracy is my brother, you know.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:16.448
He was the first person
to embrace me,

00:05:16.448 --> 00:05:18.051
because I came in
right when he left.

00:05:18.051 --> 00:05:19.485
You know what I'm saying?
-That's right.

00:05:19.485 --> 00:05:21.187
-He took me to T.G.I. Friday's
for lunch.

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:23.723
Like, "Let's go to Friday's."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:26.425
-Dude, that sounds real.
-It was very real.

00:05:26.425 --> 00:05:27.760
-The one right down the street?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.363
-Yeah, in his Cadillac
Escalade pickup truck.

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:31.897
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:33.432
He pulled it out of the garage
on 48th Street.

00:05:33.432 --> 00:05:35.434
-I love him.
-We drove around --

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:38.037
-I love him.
-50th to --

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:40.306
-You could walk --
-Back to 48th and Fifth.

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:42.675
-You could walk to it.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:44.777
-Just because he wanted us
to see his ride

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:45.912
and he wanted...
-Yeah.

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:47.580
-...to flex on
two and a half blocks.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.415
I always felt him for that.

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:51.517
-That's actually legendary.
-Stepping up.

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:53.285
-You could throw a rock and hit
T.G.I. Friday's

00:05:53.285 --> 00:05:55.020
from our building.
-Exactly.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:58.024
Next to him, you have the
legendary Dave Chappelle, man,

00:05:58.024 --> 00:06:00.159
who yesterday told me that
I was good at my job,

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:01.794
and I almost cried,
you know what I'm saying?

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:03.161
Like...
-Seriously?

00:06:03.161 --> 00:06:07.166
-The dude is -- I mean, as far
as the pinnacle of people

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:11.503
I look up to in the voice of
my generation, it's that guy.

00:06:11.503 --> 00:06:13.372
You know?
And next to him,

00:06:13.372 --> 00:06:15.441
the legendary Eddie Murphy, man,

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:18.344
the first black movie superstar,
you know?

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:20.980
And just the first person
that meant everything

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.015
to every single person
in my family.

00:06:23.015 --> 00:06:25.251
You know what I'm saying?
Everything he did, we all,

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:27.586
like, laughed really hard
and embraced.

00:06:27.586 --> 00:06:29.255
You know what I'm saying?
-Of course.

00:06:29.255 --> 00:06:31.089
-So next to him,
you have Chris Rock,

00:06:31.089 --> 00:06:32.925
who is brilliant
in his own lane.

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.994
He carved a lane so strong

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:38.063
that I don't think anybody
can say he's not

00:06:38.063 --> 00:06:39.965
probably the greatest --

00:06:39.965 --> 00:06:42.601
probably stand-up specials
that HBO ever had.

00:06:42.601 --> 00:06:44.069
You know what I'm saying?
-Ever.

00:06:44.069 --> 00:06:46.138
-That whole run that he did is
so solid and still --

00:06:46.138 --> 00:06:47.874
-Changed the game.
-Brilliant in his mind.

00:06:47.874 --> 00:06:49.508
He's killing it on "Fargo"
right now.

00:06:49.508 --> 00:06:51.076
You know what I'm saying?
-Yeah, he is, by the way.

00:06:51.076 --> 00:06:53.913
-So I could run down the credits
of those dudes all day long.

00:06:53.913 --> 00:06:55.581
And shout-out to Michael Che

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:57.249
for even writing me
in that moment, man.

00:06:57.249 --> 00:07:00.219
Like, I'm just -- like,
I'm floored when I see it.

00:07:00.219 --> 00:07:02.954
-And how about the person
holding this picture?

00:07:02.954 --> 00:07:04.357
[ Laughter ]
-And the -- and --

00:07:04.357 --> 00:07:06.292
-That's --
-If you zoom in

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:07.994
on the pink knuckles around --

00:07:07.994 --> 00:07:09.395
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:10.829
They belong to --

00:07:10.829 --> 00:07:12.331
-Zoom in on the pink knuckles.

00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:14.767
-They belong to my brother
James Fallon, who...

00:07:14.767 --> 00:07:16.369
[ Laughter ]

00:07:16.369 --> 00:07:18.070
...is probably one of
the funniest people

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.738
I've ever been around
in my entire life.

00:07:19.738 --> 00:07:21.340
-Thank you.
That's all I wanted, yeah.

00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:23.376
-Yeah, absolutely, hands down.
-Thank you, I appreciate that.

